        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 57.45,
          "end": 61.32,
          "en": "and follow the installation instructions you find there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 61.32,
          "end": 63.99,
          "en": "With that all out of the way, we can get started",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 63.99,
          "end": 65.91,
          "en": "with native device features.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 65.91,
          "end": 69.96000000000001,
          "en": "And I do want to get started with taking some images,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 69.96000000000001,
          "end": 73.68,
          "en": "to be precise, when a user adds a new place,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 73.68,
          "end": 76.53,
          "en": "the user should be able to use the device camera",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 76.53,
          "end": 79.8,
          "en": "to take an image for that place.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 79.8,
          "end": 82.38,
          "en": "For that, on that add_place screen here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 82.38,
          "end": 86.43,
          "en": "I wanna add a new input below my title here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 86.43,
          "end": 90.42,
          "en": "and that should be the ImageInput, let's say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 90.42,
          "end": 93.63,
          "en": "So an input that we can use to take an image.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 93.63,
          "end": 97.11,
          "en": "And there is no such built in input that would allow us",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 97.11,
          "end": 99.15,
          "en": "to use the camera and take an image.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 99.15,
          "end": 101.19,
          "en": "Instead, we'll have to build our own.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 101.19,
          "end": 102.50999999999999,
          "en": "So therefore that's what I'll do,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 102.50999999999999,
          "end": 105.24000000000001,
          "en": "and I'll do that here in the widgets folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 105.24000000000001,
          "end": 108.63,
          "en": "I'll add an image_input.dart file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 108.63,
          "end": 111.15,
          "en": "which will hold the ImageInput logic.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 111.15,
          "end": 115.22999999999999,
          "en": "And in there we're going to add the code to allow the user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 115.22999999999999,
          "end": 117.03,
          "en": "to open the device camera,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 117.03,
          "end": 120.12,
          "en": "show a preview of the image that was taken,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 120.12,
          "end": 124.95,
          "en": "and then also pass that image back to the add_place screen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 124.95,
          "end": 127.86,
          "en": "so that there we can use it to add it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 127.86,
          "end": 130.173,
          "en": "to the place that's being created.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 131.58,
          "end": 135.72,
          "en": "So inside here of image_input, I'll create a new class,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 135.72,
          "end": 137.94,
          "en": "and I'll name it ImageInput.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 137.94,
          "end": 140.09,
          "en": "And this will actually be a StatefulWidget,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 141.32999999999998,
          "end": 144.36,
          "en": "because here we will need to update the UI",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 144.36,
          "end": 146.223,
          "en": "and manage some state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 147.09,
          "end": 151.07999999999998,
          "en": "Now, for the moment, I'll set the ImageInput constructor",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 151.07999999999998,
          "end": 154.35,
          "en": "to a constructor that only accepts and forwards the key.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 154.35,
          "end": 157.413,
          "en": "So I don't accept any other parameters right now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 158.25,
          "end": 160.26,
          "en": "And I will add createState,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 160.26,
          "end": 162.93,
          "en": "because of course we must add this method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 162.93,
          "end": 164.49,
          "en": "to the stateful widget.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 164.49,
          "end": 166.68,
          "en": "And of course we also need that state class,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 166.68,
          "end": 169.051,
          "en": "the ImageInputState class,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 169.051,
          "end": 171.88400000000001,
          "en": "or _ImageInputState to be precise,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 173.263,
          "end": 175.347,
          "en": "where we extend State,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 175.347,
          "end": 179.993,
          "en": "and that State belongs to the ImageInput, I'll zap here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 179.993,
          "end": 183.419,
          "en": "and then here in createState, we return a new instance",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 183.419,
          "end": 185.002,
          "en": "of ImageInputState.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 186.059,
          "end": 188.79,
          "en": "And in that state class, we of course add the build method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 188.79,
          "end": 190.263,
          "en": "as we always do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 191.97,
          "end": 195.3,
          "en": "Now, in that build method, I wanna return the widgets",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 195.3,
          "end": 198.96,
          "en": "that should make up this ImageInput widget.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 198.96,
          "end": 201.18,
          "en": "And in this ImageInput widget,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 201.18,
          "end": 204.72,
          "en": "I in the end wanna display a button that can be tapped",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 204.72,
          "end": 206.64,
          "en": "to open the camera.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 206.64,
          "end": 208.89,
          "en": "And once the image has been selected,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 208.89,
          "end": 211.56,
          "en": "the button should actually be replaced",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 211.56,
          "end": 214.38,
          "en": "with a preview of that image.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 214.38,
          "end": 217.71,
          "en": "So I wanna show that image that has been picked,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 217.71,
          "end": 220.553,
          "en": "though that image should also be tappable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 220.553,
          "end": 222.69299999999998,
          "en": "so that we could replace it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 223.77,
          "end": 228.77,
          "en": "Therefore here what I'll render will be a container,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 228.84,
          "end": 231.09,
          "en": "because this Container widget will allow me",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 231.09,
          "end": 233.94,
          "en": "to control the size and also the alignment",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 233.94,
          "end": 237,
          "en": "of the content inside of the container.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 237,
          "end": 242,
          "en": "And here I'll set a height of 250 pixels.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 242.07,
          "end": 245.31,
          "en": "I'll set a width of double infinity",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 245.31,
          "end": 248.85,
          "en": "to make this container as wide as possible.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 248.85,
          "end": 250.65,
          "en": "And I'll add the child here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 250.65,
          "end": 252.84,
          "en": "And the child now, as mentioned,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 252.84,
          "end": 256.05,
          "en": "should either be a preview of the picked image",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 256.05,
          "end": 259.38,
          "en": "or a button that allows us to take an image.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 259.38,
          "end": 260.28,
          "en": "And therefore at the moment,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 260.28,
          "end": 264.36,
          "en": "I'll just set the button as the child.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 264.36,
          "end": 268.02,
          "en": "It should be a TextButton that also has an icon.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 268.02,
          "end": 270.81,
          "en": "And then here the icon I wanna use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 270.81,
          "end": 275.81,
          "en": "is of course the Icon widget where I use the camera icon,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 277.05,
          "end": 281.25,
          "en": "which sounds fitting for this purpose of opening the camera.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 281.25,
          "end": 283.8,
          "en": "Then the label is a Text widget",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 283.8,
          "end": 285.25,
          "en": "where I say ('Take Picture').",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 287.7,
          "end": 290.25,
          "en": "And then of course, we also need onPressed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 290.25,
          "end": 293.043,
          "en": "where at the moment I have an empty anonymous function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 294,
          "end": 295.86,
          "en": "Now I wanna make sure that this button",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 295.86,
          "end": 298.08,
          "en": "is centered inside of that container,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 298.08,
          "end": 299.61,
          "en": "which has a fixed height.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 299.61,
          "end": 302.49,
          "en": "And to make sure that this is the case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 302.49,
          "end": 306.36,
          "en": "I will therefore add the alignment parameter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 306.36,
          "end": 309.18,
          "en": "and set this to Alignment.center,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 309.18,
          "end": 312.24,
          "en": "which will center the child horizontally",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 312.24,
          "end": 314.973,
          "en": "and vertically inside of this container.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 316.59,
          "end": 320.22,
          "en": "So with that, we have this container and this button.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 320.22,
          "end": 324.48,
          "en": "If we go back to add_place, we can now use this here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 324.48,
          "end": 329.16,
          "en": "So here I'll add my ImageInput widget like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 329.16,
          "end": 331.89,
          "en": "And of course at the moment it doesn't do anything yet,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 331.89,
          "end": 334.2,
          "en": "but this will change later.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 334.2,
          "end": 336.9,
          "en": "If I save this and I go to this screen,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 336.9,
          "end": 340.59000000000003,
          "en": "I now have this Take Picture button here which I can tap.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 340.59000000000003,
          "end": 343.35,
          "en": "And as mentioned, eventually this will be replaced",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 343.35,
          "end": 345.453,
          "en": "with the image that we did select.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 346.89,
          "end": 350.61,
          "en": "Now, I also want to add a little border around this input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 350.61,
          "end": 353.34000000000003,
          "en": "to make it clear where it starts and ends.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 353.34000000000003,
          "end": 356.52,
          "en": "And for that I can go to my ImageInput widget again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 356.52,
          "end": 357.75,
          "en": "and there to the container,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 357.75,
          "end": 362.75,
          "en": "and set the decoration parameter to BoxDecoration,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 363.09,
          "end": 366.15,
          "en": "because this BoxDecoration constructive function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 366.15,
          "end": 368.553,
          "en": "then allows me to set a border.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 369.51,
          "end": 371.79,
          "en": "And here we can then create a new border",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 371.79,
          "end": 374.82,
          "en": "with Flutter's Border clause,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 374.82,
          "end": 376.86,
          "en": "where I could now manually configure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 376.86,
          "end": 379.65,
          "en": "the different sides of that rectangle.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 379.65,
          "end": 382.59,
          "en": "So the different borders on the different sides.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 382.59,
          "end": 385.65,
          "en": "Or we use the special all constructor function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 385.65,
          "end": 388.53,
          "en": "which allows us to configure all the borders",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 388.53,
          "end": 391.17,
          "en": "for all sides in one step.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 391.17,
          "end": 394.17,
          "en": "And here I'll give all my borders a width of one,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 394.17,
          "end": 399.17,
          "en": "and set a color of Theme.of(context).colorScheme.primary.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 402.42,
